# Ignore local Claude state (settings.local.json, caches) but SHARE project
# slash commands: they are part of the repo's workflow (/app-review drives the
# docs/app-review rotation) and are useless if every clone must recreate them.
# Must be `.claude/*` not `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a path through an
# excluded parent directory, so the negations below would never apply.
#
# The SessionStart hook is shared for the same reason, and a stronger one: it
# stands up MariaDB and Redis so a web session can run the DB-backed half of
# the test suite. Without it those 1000+ tests do not fail, they ERROR out of
# fixture setup, and the summary line still reads as a pass. Recreating that
# per clone is how a session reports green on a suite that never ran.
# settings.local.json stays ignored — it is personal, and is not re-included.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json

# Playwright
/frontend/test-results/
/frontend/playwright-report/
/frontend/blob-report/
/frontend/.playwright/

# Documentation screenshot capture report (regenerated by scripts/screenshots/capture.mjs)
/scripts/screenshots/capture-report.json

# Stryker mutation testing (regenerated by `npx stryker run stryker.pilot.json`)
/frontend/reports/
/backend/reports/
/frontend/.stryker-tmp/

# Scratch reproductions and lint/type probes.
#
# Review and verification agents write throwaway files into the tree to prove a
# finding — a failing repro, a probe that checks whether a lint rule actually
# fires. They are debugging instruments, not tests: they routinely carry a
# deliberate always-fail sentinel (`toEqual('SHOWME')`) to dump an observed
# value, so one committed by accident is a guaranteed-red CI run. Two reached
# `git add -A` on 2026-08-30 and were only caught by the pre-commit hook.
#
# Ignored rather than merely remembered, because the failure mode is silent and
# the cost of a miss is a broken main. Keep the names distinctive so a genuine
# test is never swallowed: a real one is never called `__scratch` or `__probe`.
__scratch*
__probe*
__lintprobe*
scratchRepro*
